# The Flentrop of 1958, Adolphus Busch Hall: a stop
# for dacvoice (voices/README.md, "Stops"). The division's lines (n,
# frame, envelope, chiff) are the same in each of its stops, so they mix.
name Mixtuur II
family Rugpositief
n 10
frame 8
start 18 dB
attack 0.012 s
peak 0 dB
decay 0 dB/s
sustain 0 dB
release 0.05 s
chiff 0.010 s 16 dB 2 12
# Rugpositief: two principal ranks, 1 1/3 and 1 foot, each breaking back an
# octave at C5 (zone 4).
harmonics 1 1.0  2 0.4  3 0.2  4 0.1
rank 6 1.0 break 4
rank 8 1.0 break 4
level 2 dB
# The voicing (voices/README.md, "The voicing"): the speech by the pipe's
# size, and Busch Hall, where the organ stands.
rise 10
room busch
# The celeste: a second read of the table at half the rate, 2 cents
# sharp, a rank a little off the unison.
celeste 2
